WEBVTT

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.810
You did yourself proud yesterday, Rudeus.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.520
No, I'm sorry.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.600
What happened was my fault.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.600
Still, I don't understand.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.400
I know why they abducted Eris,
but why me as well?

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.980
There are many uses for
a member of the Greyrat bloodline.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.690
Both politically and physically. See?

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.730
I... see?

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.980
By the way, I assume you
understand. You must not...

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.730
Yes, I understand. Ghislaine did it all, right?

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:40.900
Good.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.560
Officially, Ghislaine dealt
with the kidnapping on her own.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.770
To let people know that
we have a Sword King here,

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.310
and show the Greyrats' strength.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:56.190
And apparently it would be bad if
the "other" Greyrats knew about me.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:01.650
I don't really get it, but it
must be political wrangling.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:02.690
Hilda.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.270
Good morning, dear.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:09.560
This is Paul's son.
I've hired him as Eris's new tutor.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:14.150
It's a pleasure to meet you.
I am Rudeus Greyrat.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.690
She must be Philip's wife.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.190
It looks like she doesn't like me.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.230
Why?

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.940
Is Paul's son here?!

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.520
Pleased to meet you. I am Rudeus Greyrat.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.560
You're polite for Paul's boy!

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.100
You may stay in this manor!

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.560
Master Rudeus, that is
the current lord of Fittoa,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.940
Lord Sauros Boreas Greyrat.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:50.520
My father.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.150
I hear you saved Eris!

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.020
Oh, no, it wasn't me. Ghislaine...

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:59.270
Are you trying to lie to me, boy?!

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:00.310
H-Huh?

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:03.980
N-No, sir! Lord Philip told me to...

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.350
Philip!

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.350
Yes, Father.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.100
Huh?

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:16.690
Ingrate! Is that any way to
treat your daughter's savior?!

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:20.600
Father, Rudeus has Greyrat blood.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:26.980
Rather than a mere show of gratitude,
I hope to thank him warmly, as family.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.650
As long as you have a plan!

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.350
Thank you very much.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.150
What the...?

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.850
So, he won't apologize for the punch?

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:40.020
Come to think of it, Eris never
apologized to me, either.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.980
Not that I really mind.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.730
Rudeus! I have a request!

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.600
Y-Yes, sir!

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.810
Teach Eris magic!

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:55.480
She says she can't get the
spells you cast out of her head!

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.600
Of course I...

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.730
Wow. He's just like Eris.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:04.560
Maybe Eris got like that by imitating this guy?

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.100
I think Lady Eris ought to ask me that herself.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.350
What?!

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:15.560
Wh-What if she grows up to be too proud
to ask for what she wants politely?

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.400
Oh, well said!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.600
You're quite right!

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:26.730
Eris!

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.100
Coming!

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.270
Grandfather! Did you talk to him?!

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:40.350
Eris! If you want to ask for
something, ask for it yourself!

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.850
What?! But you said you'd ask him for me!

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.940
Eris!

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.690
P-Please...

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.400
Is that any way to ask for something?!

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.850
You're one to talk.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.600
P-Please teach Eris magic, meow.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.230
Huh?

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.560
Oh, yes. That's the way.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.400
Of course he'll do it. Isn't that right, Rudeus?

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.520
You have to stick out your hips more.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.230
The masters are fond of beast people.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.650
That pose is an imitation of drooping ears.

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:32.480
I don't need reading, writing, or math, meow!

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.520
Just magic, meow!

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:40.310
Is that any way to ask for something?!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.100
All right.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.100
Yes!

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:16.020
Use your legs more! Not just your hands!

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:22.690
Let the great protection of fire
be on the place thou seekest.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:25.730
I call the bold heat of a torch here and now!

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:27.850
Fireball!

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.810
Yes! I did it!

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:09.930
Mushoku Tensei: Jobless Reincarnation

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.730
Next, you do this.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:15.900
Eight plus five equals 13. Simple, right?

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.690
Yes, I see.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.560
I kind of get it now.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.310
Look, look! Rudeus!

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:26.310
One day, I'll make huge fireworks like you do!

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:29.150
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:36.650
I wish you were that enthusiastic
about reading, writing, or math.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:46.690
Again?

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:50.810
Eris, where are you? Class isn't over.

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:50.810
I've been her tutor for a month now.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.310
Eris won't listen to my lessons.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.060
Eris!

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.520
Try to convince her, she runs.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:58.480
Eris, come out!

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:58.480
Try to catch her, she punches me, then runs.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:02.900
If I chase her, she comes back to
punch me again, then runs again.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.440
It's always like this with
reading, writing, and math.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.900
She looks like an angel when she's sleeping.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.940
Eris, you'll catch a cold.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:24.940
Wake up, or I'll attack you.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:35.270
She's still a AA,

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:39.730
but with diligence,
she could become an E or bigger.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.770
Please wake up, My Lady.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:48.230
It's time for your fun, fun lessons.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:58.810
Sound asleep, huh? Oh well.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:02.810
Bad girls can't complain
if someone takes their panties off.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.650
H-Here it comes!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.480
Set play out of frame advantage.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:35.650
Looks like she completely outplayed me.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.770
It's hopeless. I'll ask Ghislaine for help.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:47.190
She must know something about managing Eris.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.770
I'm bored now!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:09.190
I used to think that a sword was all I needed.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:13.690
My party, "The Fangs of the
Black Wolf," had six members:

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:20.730
Two swordsmen, a fighter, and a thief,
plus one mage and one cleric.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:24.940
I let the others handle getting
and handing out supplies.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:25.940
Adventurers!

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.060
She's hooked!

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:30.400
Were my mother and father
in that party with you?

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:33.770
Yeah. It was seven years ago now.

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.810
I thought that would be it.

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:40.980
So, Ghislaine, have you ever been in
trouble because you couldn't do math?

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.690
Yeah, loads of it.

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:46.150
After Paul and Zenith got married,

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:51.980
I traveled alone,
but I couldn't calculate money.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.600
I went ten days without food or drink.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.520
I thought I'd die.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:10:01.600
I couldn't bear it and ate monster shit,
but it gave me the runs.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:06.560
While I endured nausea, stomachache, and
diarrhea, monsters swarmed around me.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.850
Hearing about it makes <i>my</i> stomach ache.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:15.350
That's why I want to learn math.
I'm counting on you.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:24.230
Rudeus! Hurry up and get on with the lesson!

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:33.810
I wish you were this proactive in <i>my</i> classes!

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:37.020
Learn to step in! Watch your opponent!

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:42.400
Step in faster than your opponent,
read their moves, then swing your sword!

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:48.650
Keep your eyes open!

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:52.650
If you don't step in first,
get out of the path of their sword!

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.190
Watch their feet and eyes
to predict what they'll do!

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.520
Rudeus! Don't think with your head!

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:03.440
Think about stepping in first and swinging!

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:06.020
Do you want me to think or not?!

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:08.190
Eris! Don't stop!

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.850
He hasn't given up yet!

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.270
Right!

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.230
Give me a break.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:23.060
You've got a way to go, Rudeus!

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.440
Don't get conceited.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:29.060
You've been learning the
sword longer, and you're older.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:32.980
I know that! And Rudeus has his magic, too!

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:34.270
Right.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:39.810
But Rudeus, your movements get
sluggish when you're being attacked.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:45.230
I get scared when someone's in
my face and seriously attacking.

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:47.230
What?! That's pathetic!

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.230
That's why people look down on you!

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:52.230
No, Rudeus is a mage. He's better off that way.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.770
Really? I guess he can't help it, then!

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.850
What did she hit me for?

00:11:56.850 --> 00:12:00.480
Sorry, but I don't know how
to fix your legs flinching.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:01.940
Fix that yourself.

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.100
I will.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:05.350
Rudeus! Get up already!

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:06.770
We'll go another round!

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:10.560
You could hold back a little, you know?

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.850
You're just too weak!

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:14.850
I figured.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:17.310
Okay, begin!

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.350
Ow, ow, ow...

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.520
Every day is exhausting.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:36.350
Still, I've got to prepare tomorrow's lessons.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:42.690
Ugh! This is such a pain!

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:47.690
Who knew earning money was so much work?

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:57.440
But I've got to keep at it so I can
go to Magic University with Sylphie.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:01.440
Okay!

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:04.400
Eris actually pays attention in class now!

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.850
I just need to keep this up for five years!

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:22.980
Or so I thought, when
Eris started acting up again.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.520
I completely forgot!

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:37.850
Of course! She has no time off!

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.150
Hurry!

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.810
Come on, let's go!

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:45.850
Eris, I know I'm repeating myself,

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:49.020
but absolutely do not wander off alone in town.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:53.690
It would be awful if you got
abducted again. Mentally speaking.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:59.850
I know, so let's get going already!

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:02.900
That aside, that dress...

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.190
They do say "fine feathers make a fine bird."

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:14.060
It looks lovely on you, My Lady.

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:15.730
I'm going!

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:17.980
What's her problem?

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:36.310
I'm told Roa is the largest city in the
Fittoa Region of the Asura Kingdom.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:40.230
Beautiful streets surrounded
by magnificent ramparts.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:45.940
Seeing them up close, I can't help
feeling excited. What boy wouldn't?

00:14:57.690 --> 00:15:00.810
So, an apple costs one Asura copper piece.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:04.850
You there, young sir!

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:06.020
You mean me?

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:10.060
You're finely dressed.
Are you from the lord's manor?

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:10.980
Yes, why?

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:16.060
Then, I have an extremely valuable item
to show you. What do you say?

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.060
What is this?

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:26.310
A prized medicine from Asura Palace.
I got it in this morning.

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:29.520
One sip lets you go ten
times without pulling out.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:35.350
Give a woman a sip, and she'll be drooling
and spreading her legs, they say.

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:40.900
It would be the perfect present
for your daddy! What do you say?

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:38.730
A-An aphrodisiac! Ten gold pieces?!

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.900
Better write that down.

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:45.190
What's that writing?! I can't read it!

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:47.940
It's my notes. It only matters
that I can read them.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:50.230
Tell me what you're writing!

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:51.850
What a little tyrant.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:54.020
The names and prices of goods.

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:56.230
What do you want to know those for?!

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:58.940
Researching market prices is basic MMO strategy.

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:01.520
"MM"...? What's that?!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:04.190
Here, look at this.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.310
Something that cost five
large coppers across the street

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:09.980
is being sold here for four.

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:12.190
Now, a question:

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:17.100
If you haggled the price here down to
three large coppers and sold it there for four,

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:18.900
how much would you make?

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:20.440
Huh?! Umm...

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.310
Five minus three plus four is...

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.150
Six coppers!

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:26.230
What kind of math is that?

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:28.770
Bzzt! Wrong answer.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:31.690
Four minus three equals one large copper.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.100
That's right, Ghislaine!

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:34.480
I did it.

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:36.020
I-I knew that!

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:37.310
Did you really?

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:42.190
I-If I started with ten large coppers,
I'd end up with 11, right?

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:44.190
Does she really get it?

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:46.230
I'll praise her anyway.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.150
Eris is proud, so praise helps her improve.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.940
Oh, you got that one right.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.100
Wow, you're clever, Eris.

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:55.730
Naturally!

00:16:55.730 --> 00:17:00.650
So you see, there are benefits
to knowing what things cost.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:59.530
Excuse me, young sir...

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:04.060
Do you see how useful arithmetic can be now?

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.900
Yes, I understand!

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.150
Yeah.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:14.650
A botanical dictionary, seven gold pieces.

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:19.690
I think one gold piece is around
100,000 yen, so it costs about 700,000 yen.

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:23.520
Talk about pricey. What did Mom
have to do to afford that?

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:24.810
What are you looking at?!

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:28.400
Oh, I just thought I might
find an interesting book.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.310
I could buy you one, if you like!

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:34.900
That's easy to say, but do
you actually have money?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:37.150
Grandfather will pay for me!

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:40.900
I figured. I can't let her act spoiled.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:42.770
Still, I do want a book.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:45.100
I <i>really</i> want a book!

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:46.350
No thank you.

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:47.560
Why?!

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.270
Because it's not your money to spend.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:51.940
What do you mean?!

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:56.520
Do you know how much
I get paid every month, Eris?

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.810
About five gold pieces?

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.270
Two silver pieces.

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.230
That's too little!

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:04.690
And Ghislaine?!

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:06.440
I get two gold pieces.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:07.440
See?!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.560
"See" what?

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:15.150
Ghislaine has the rank of Sword King,
and she doubles as your bodyguard.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.440
It's natural that she's paid more.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.690
Wh-What would I get paid, then?

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:24.020
No more than one silver piece, at the very most.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.520
I appreciate the sentiment,

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:31.900
but you should wait until you have
your own money to buy people gifts.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:33.770
All right, fine.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.190
She's unusually quiet.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:39.400
If only she always acted like this.

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:43.020
That was probably Eris's attempt at gratitude.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:48.230
Well, when we get back, let's ask
Lord Philip to give you an allowance.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.980
You mean it?!

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.440
Whoa!

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:16.850
Never seen it before?

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:19.770
You know what that is,
Raide--I mean, Ghislaine?!

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:21.440
You don't?

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:25.230
That's the flying fortress of Perugius,
the Armored Dragon King.

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:26.850
Perugius?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:32.400
Perugius is one of the three heroes
who beat the Demon-God Laplace!

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.650
Laplace?

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:36.020
What, you don't know about him either?

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:40.810
Laplace was a super evil guy
who tried to wipe out humans!

00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:41.980
Huh?

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:46.600
I feel like I've heard this
story before. But where?

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:49.150
Perugius is super strong!

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:55.100
So, he and his 12 servants went
after Laplace and beat him up!

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:57.100
Oh, I know.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:20:02.230
It was in a book at home.
I thought it must be a fairy tale.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:05.350
You know a lot, My Lady.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.440
This is the year 414 of the
Armored Dragon Calendar.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:13.730
The calendar was named in honor
of Perugius defeating Laplace.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:14.730
Wow.

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:16.810
You've got a lot to learn, Rudeus!

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:21.900
It's been flying for 400 years
since the war with Laplace ended?

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:27.150
Is this Perugius guy
really still alive up there?

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:30.810
Still, I'd like to go there someday.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:37.650
I did it!

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:40.270
Let me see.

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:43.020
Eris's mood has improved since
we gave her one day off a week.

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:43.310
Good. Well done, Eris.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:45.850
Giving her time to relax was the right move.

00:20:43.310 --> 00:20:45.850
Yes!

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:48.560
By the way, Rudeus!

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:53.940
M-M-My Lady, why do you have this?!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.150
You looked like you wanted it!

00:20:56.150 --> 00:21:00.150
Thanks to you, Lady Eris gets an allowance now.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:03.230
I even calculated the change right!

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:06.150
Thank you very much.

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:08.560
I'm glad your studies are paying off.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:11.100
Now, let's get back to your lesson!

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:14.650
By the way, what's that medicine for?!

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:17.980
Okay, I've got a tough problem for you today.

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.900
Let's see if you two can solve it!

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:23.440
Don't change the subject! Tell me!

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:24.850
Bye!

00:21:24.850 --> 00:21:27.350
Ghislaine, capture Rudeus!

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:28.560
Sure.

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:32.940
L-Let go! I haven't done
anything to feel guilty a--

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:34.350
Ah.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:40.650
My million-yen aphrodisiac!

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:42.440
Did you say "aphrodisiac"?

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:44.190
What's an "aphrodisiac"?

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:47.600
Uh, umm, you see...

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:53.150
Wait!

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:57.060
I had a hell of a time
talking my way out of that.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:01.020
This violent girl and meathead
swordswoman are infamous.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:00.770
Come on, spit it out!

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:03.520
What's an "aphrodisiac"?!

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:05.310
Still, it does look like
their studies are paying off.

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:06.810
Come on, tell me!

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:08.810
I think I'll celebrate that for now.

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:11.930
Episode 6

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:11.930
A Day Off in Roa

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:46.940
Next time

00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:46.940
What Lies Beyond Effort
